.TH JENT_SET_FIPS_FAILURE_CALLBACK 3 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "Library Functions Manual"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jent_set_fips_failure_callback \- health test failure callback of the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH LIBRARY
Jitter RNG library
.RI ( libjitterentropy ", " \-ljitterentropy ).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <jitterentropy.h>
.sp
.BI "typedef void (*jent_fips_failure_cb)(struct rand_data *" ec ",
.BI "                                     unsigned int " health_failure );
.sp
.BI "int jent_set_fips_failure_callback(jent_fips_failure_cb " cb ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR jent_set_fips_failure_callback ()
allows the caller to set a callback that is invoked by the
Jitter RNG when a health test failure is detected. The callback
specified with the parameter
.BR cb
to the API function receives the Jitter RNG state with the parameter
.BR ec
and the FIPS health test failure with the parameter
.BR health_failure ,
a bit mask of
.B JENT_RCT_FAILURE
(1),
.B JENT_APT_FAILURE
(2),
.B JENT_LAG_FAILURE
(4) and
.B JENT_RCT_MEM_FAILURE
(8) for an intermittent failure, and the same bits shifted by
.B JENT_PERMANENT_FAILURE_SHIFT
(16) for a permanent one:
.BR JENT_RCT_FAILURE_PERMANENT ,
.BR JENT_APT_FAILURE_PERMANENT ,
.B JENT_LAG_FAILURE_PERMANENT
and
.BR JENT_RCT_MEM_FAILURE_PERMANENT ,
formed with
.BR JENT_PERMANENT_FAILURE ().
.LP
The callback is invoked in FIPS mode only - with
.BR JENT_FORCE_FIPS ,
.B JENT_NTG1
or the FIPS mode of the system - every time the health test results of an
instance are checked while failure bits stand, with every bit then standing.
As the bits of an instance stay set, it may be invoked more than once for the
same failure. The results are checked during generation, and also during the
startup entropy collection that every
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3)
and every recovery of
.BR jent_read_entropy_safe ()
runs on the new collector - where an intermittent failure makes the startup
replace that collector in turn - and during the timer tests of
.BR jent_entropy_init (3)
and
.BR jent_entropy_init_ex (),
which always run their health tests as in FIPS mode, on a collector of their
own.
The
.I ec
the callback is handed is valid for the duration of the call only: a failure
may be followed by a reallocation, which frees it moments later, and during a
startup or a timer test the collector is not one the caller holds - nor, in
the startup of a new allocation, one with an identifier yet. Anything
the callback needs afterwards - the identifier, a status document of
.BR jent_status (3)
- has to be copied out while it runs, not kept as a pointer.
.LP
This function must be called before
.BR jent_entropy_init (3)
as after this call, the change of the callback is denied.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR jent_set_fips_failure_callback ()
returns 0 on success and
.I \-EAGAIN
once an initialization has run.
.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
See
.B THREAD SAFETY
in
.BR jitterentropy (3)
for the details.
.ad l
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb
lx l.
Interface	Thread safety
T{
\%\fBjent_set_fips_failure_callback\fP()
T}	MT-Unsafe init
.TE
.ad
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jent_entropy_init (3),
.BR jent_read_entropy (3),
.BR jent_status (3),
.BR jitterentropy (3)
